UniFi OS Server installer — pinned private-API model source (fetched at build)
==============================================================================

This file is the PIN MANIFEST, not the installer. The installer is a build
input: fetched (or reused from a local copy) by ./fetch.sh into a cache OUTSIDE
the repo, verified against the pinned SHA-256 below, and never committed. The
values live in ./pin.env (the single source of truth); this file explains them.

Release:     UniFi OS Server 5.1.15, linux-x64
Network app: 10.4.57 (image build arg UNIFI_VERSION=10.4.57-34628-1)
Download:    https://fw-download.ubnt.com/data/unifi-os-server/24e0-linux-x64-5.1.15-926621de-c9d7-48cd-8921-a0ff3eebd3f4.15-x64
Size:        874,927,011 bytes
Checksum:    sha256 04c8e401eb34330fe99d94f35aa351e0e0e97895f0d9a4b459ff34fb50cad2bb
Listed by:   https://fw-update.ubnt.com/api/firmware (product unifi-os-server)

fetch.sh checks the PINNED checksum above, never fw-update's own field, so a
changed listing cannot change what the build reads.

What the build reads (provider/pkg/uos; nothing is executed, nothing raw is
written into the repo):
  installer (ELF) + appended ZIP -> image.tar (OCI, docker-archive layout)
    -> the layer holding usr/lib/unifi/lib/ace.jar (found by content)
      -> ace.jar -> BOOT-INF/lib/internal-dependencies.jar
         - classes: Spring/Jackson/Jakarta annotations -> v2 route table + DTO models
         - api/fields/*.json -> classic /api/s/{site}/rest kinds
         - sensitive_metadata.json -> secret marking
      -> webapps/ROOT/api-docs/integration.json (the official spec; its SHA-256
         must equal SPEC_SHA256 in ../openapi/pin.env: the pin tie)
The output is build/uos/model.json (gitignored).

Cache
-----
${UNIFI_UOS_CACHE:-$HOME/.cache/pulumi-unifi/uos}/<sha256>/installer
Set UOS_INSTALLER=<path> to reuse a local copy (checked, then hard-linked or
copied into the cache) instead of downloading 875 MB.

